For law-enforcement high-risk AI systems (Annex III points 1, 6 and 7 in the areas of law enforcement, migration, asylum and border control management), the testing is registered in the secure non-public section of the EU database according to Article 49(4), point (d). That provision specifies the applicable information as points 1, 2, 3 and 5 of Annex IX.

Accordingly, the registration must include Annex IX points 1, 2, 3 and 5:
- 1. The Union-wide unique single identification number of the testing;
- 2. The name and contact details of the provider or prospective provider and of the deployers involved;
- 3. A brief description of the AI system, its intended purpose, and other identifying information;
- 5. Information on the suspension or termination of the testing.
